{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1793092125","published":"2026-10-27T09:28:57Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:31:43.002634443Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-35189","CVE-2026-72897","CVE-2026-75804","CVE-2026-84782"],"summary":"openssl: Fix of 4 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-84782: reset the DTLS retransmission read position to the start of\n  the message and skip retransmission while a handshake write is suspended,\n  so a retransmit can no longer read past the message buffer or corrupt the\n  state of the suspended write\n- CVE-2026-72897: resize the signature algorithm validity flags when\n  SSL_set_SSL_CTX() switches context mid-handshake, so a replacement context\n  with more provider signature algorithms can no longer cause out-of-bounds\n  heap access\n- CVE-2026-75804: enforce the QUIC connection-level flow control limit for\n  stream data, so a peer can no longer make the receiver buffer far more data\n  than the advertised connection window\n- CVE-2026-35189: compute the full name of relative CRL distribution points\n  only when matching a CRL instead of for every parsed certificate, so a\n  crafted certificate can no longer cause excessive heap growth","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openssl","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/openssl?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:3.2.2-7.el9_6.tuxcare.1.els13"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1793092125.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssl-devel","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/openssl-devel?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:3.2.2-7.el9_6.tuxcare.1.els13"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1793092125.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssl-libs","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","